WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.620
From a shocking major character death, to
extra-deadly demobats that would have killed

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:10.660
Steve, and a big change to the Mind Flayer
reveal in the finale, there were some fascinating

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:13.610
moments and scenes cut from Stranger Things
4!

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:17.970
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm revealing the deleted scenes

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:22.310
and alternate ending you never got to see
in the fourth season of Stranger Things.

00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.840
Spoilers ahead, of course, so take care.

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.900
In the Season 4 finale, everything goes horribly
wrong when Vecna claims Max as his fourth

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:33.320
victim, opening the four gates to the Upside
Down.

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.640
Although Max briefly died, Eleven managed
to bring her back, though she was left in

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.640
a coma.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:43.400
The Duffer Brothers have revealed, however,
that in the season's original ending Max died

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:48.070
permanently, but they changed their minds
about this as they "wanted to end [on] a little

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:49.710
more of a question mark".

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:55.070
Obviously, I'm glad Max survived her deadly
encounter, and given how much Season 4 channels

00:00:55.070 --> 00:01:00.390
The Empire Strikes Back, I think her comatose
state is akin to Han Solo ending up frozen

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:01.390
in carbonite.

00:01:01.390 --> 00:01:06.920
In other words, it's something she'll surely
recover from in the fifth and final season.

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:12.899
The Upside Down's demobats introduced in Season
4 were fearsome predators and with their hive-mind

00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:15.960
connection to Vecna, they could act as the
villain's spies.

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:20.999
Fan favourite Eddie tragically died from his
injuries after being attacked by the creatures,

00:01:20.999 --> 00:01:25.720
but originally the flying monsters were going
to be even more deadly.

00:01:25.720 --> 00:01:30.729
According to Stranger Things concept artist
Michael Maher Jr, the initially approved version

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:36.210
of the bats had "serrated tail tentacles that
were […] meant to wrap and then cut flesh."

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:41.260
If the demobats we saw in the show had been
equipped with this razor-sharp tail, it seems

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:45.590
like they could have easily killed Steve when
one of them wrapped its tail around his neck

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:49.530
and began strangling him after he was taken
into the Upside Down.

00:01:49.530 --> 00:01:54.319
On top of that, another even more gruesome
version of the demobat was considered "whose

00:01:54.319 --> 00:01:57.079
head and body would split open horizontally."

00:01:57.079 --> 00:02:00.950
I think this design would have felt a little
similar to the demodogs and demogorgons whose

00:02:00.950 --> 00:02:05.469
heads open up, although seeing the whole of
the demobat's body open up would have been

00:02:05.469 --> 00:02:06.609
pretty horrifying!

00:02:06.609 --> 00:02:11.689
By the way, the original design for the demobats
was based on the parasitic Mynock bats from

00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:15.950
Star Wars which attack the Millennium Falcon
in The Empire Strikes Back.

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:21.170
Fans have been heart-broken over the death
of Eddie, but the season very nearly ended

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.909
with another big death as well as the Duffer
Brothers have revealed that originally Dmitri,

00:02:25.909 --> 00:02:29.510
aka Enzo, didn't make it out of the season
alive.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:33.439
The Russian prison guard became friends with
Hopper when they were imprisoned together

00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:36.140
after being given up by the treacherous Yuri.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:40.560
Dmitri was crucial in changing Yuri's mind
about sabotaging the helicopter, which in

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:45.239
turn ensured Hopper, Joyce and Murray could
finally escape the Russian prison after they

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:47.550
destroyed the demodogs and Demogorgon.

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:52.280
Perhaps killing off a Russian good guy felt
too similar to Alexei dying at the end of

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:54.750
Season 3, so the Duffers changed it.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:59.590
After all, from what we saw in season 4, there
wasn't any major narrative need to kill off

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:02.540
Dimitri, so the change feels like a sensible
one.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.640
It's also possible the Duffers still have
a little something planned for a Russian storyline

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:11.379
in Season 5, so they kept him alive, given
how he told Yuri that Russia could be under

00:03:11.379 --> 00:03:16.900
threat from the Upside Down as well.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.030
When asked on the Happy Sad Confused podcast
whether Eddie was always destined to have

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:25.800
a single-season arc on the show, the Duffer
Brothers explained that even if he had survived

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.620
his encounter with the Demobats, his character
was still doomed and he would have wound up

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.620
in jail.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:34.599
Because nobody in Hawkins would have accepted
a "supernatural explanation" for what happened

00:03:34.599 --> 00:03:38.620
to Chrissy, Fred and Patrick, and he was still
being demonised at the end.

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:43.360
Sadly, the Duffers said Eddie's plan to finally
graduate was never a realistic one, and he

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:47.030
was "hurtling towards doom" through all of
Season 4.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:51.830
An incredible piece of concept art which sadly
didn't make it into the final cut was of this

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.920
moment when Eleven sends Henry through an
inter-dimensional tear from the Rainbow Room.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:01.910
The point-of-view here is from the Hellscape
that One falls into and it's a beautiful shot

00:04:01.910 --> 00:04:04.030
that would have been fantastic to see.

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:09.420
After One was thrown into the Hellscape, he
arrived in a strange new world where he came

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:13.859
across a swarming mass of dark particles that
were seemingly alive.

00:04:13.859 --> 00:04:18.609
With his powers, he shaped these into the
giant spider form we know as the Mind Flayer,

00:04:18.609 --> 00:04:23.250
that he would go on to control and use to
manipulate Will in Season 2.

00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:27.550
However, Maher has explained that in early
concepts of that scene, in order to create

00:04:27.550 --> 00:04:32.500
the Mind Flayer, One actually had to extract
the particles out of floating boulders.

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:37.800
By contrast, the final TV show reveals that
the particles already existed as a separate

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.470
entity before Henry ever went into that dimension.

00:04:41.470 --> 00:04:45.479
The Upside Down has probably been around for
thousands of years.

00:04:45.479 --> 00:04:47.080
Millions.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:51.419
And that change might also imply that the
particles in this dimension, as well as the

00:04:51.419 --> 00:04:56.330
Demogorgon creatures which were already living
there when Henry arrived, weren't malicious

00:04:56.330 --> 00:05:02.159
until he came along and transformed them into
a malevolent force for his own ends.

00:05:02.159 --> 00:05:07.530
Concept artist Maher also revealed that the
floating rocks in this dimension are "an asteroid

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:12.599
field" operating under "an altered state of
gravity", and his initial idea was that "the

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:17.570
Mind Flayer particles were an anti-gravity
element that would lift the boulders into

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.710
the air", making the rocks fall upwards.

00:05:20.710 --> 00:05:25.810
This sounds like the particles that One discovers
are a kind of fundamental force that governs

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.630
things in this other dimension.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:31.880
Apparently, the idea was abandoned in the
end as Maher says it "would have taken too

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.599
long to explain in the context of the story".

00:05:34.599 --> 00:05:39.530
Also, the dimension's original look in this
concept art was a lot darker, whereas it had

00:05:39.530 --> 00:05:43.600
a yellowish-orange hue and lighting in the
final version.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:48.660
And Vecna's Mind Lair – where he torments
Max and Eleven and stores the bodies of his

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:52.220
victims – originally had some strikingly
different designs.

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:57.410
According to Maher, this one is "a large vortex
where fragments of the house were dissolving

00:05:57.410 --> 00:06:00.800
along with spires containing rotted victims.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:02.169
Everything would be moving.

00:06:02.169 --> 00:06:05.129
Slowly swirling in a circular motion."

00:06:05.129 --> 00:06:09.879
And in this version of the villain's lair,
Vecna dragged his victims across a blood-soaked

00:06:09.879 --> 00:06:13.770
space towards a huge stone structure in the
background.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:17.940
Maher has said that this idea – and the
look of the Mind Lair in general – is influenced

00:06:17.940 --> 00:06:22.600
by the paintings of the dystopian surrealist
Polish artist Beksiński.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:26.889
And this similar shot of a vast landscape
with Vecna dragging his victim to a towering

00:06:26.889 --> 00:06:32.010
slab of rock on top of an enormous mound was
inspired by the sci-fi psychological thriller

00:06:32.010 --> 00:06:37.660
The Cell, which features scenes literally
entering a killer's twisted mind and dreamscape.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.690
In this other horrifying version, there's
a slimy web of interconnected vines suspending

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.590
three of Vecna's victims over some kind of
altar.

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:49.370
And it looks like he was dragging his fourth
victim over to the spot.

00:06:49.370 --> 00:06:54.220
There's a real spider's web feel about this
design, which is fitting, of course, given

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.380
Henry's love of black widow spiders as a child.

00:06:57.380 --> 00:07:02.659
And in these earlier versions, Max was suspended
in the air via Vecna's vines, rather than

00:07:02.659 --> 00:07:05.040
against a column as happened in the show.

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:10.569
This is more akin to how Vecna himself levitates
via a web of vines whenever he's projecting

00:07:10.569 --> 00:07:13.500
his consciousness outside his physical body.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:19.220
By the way, Maher also revealed that the swirling
haze in Vecna's lair is meant to reference

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:24.050
the storm in Billy's mind that Eleven saw
when she reached into his memories in Season

00:07:24.050 --> 00:07:25.099
3.

00:07:25.099 --> 00:07:30.610
And an early concept of Vecna's attic had
him lifted into the air by vines coming mostly

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:31.979
from the floor.

00:07:31.979 --> 00:07:36.909
This later morphed into the final idea where
he was suspended instead from the sides and

00:07:36.909 --> 00:07:41.610
the ceiling, deliberately creating the effect
of a spider's web and how a spider waits in

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:44.190
its web to trap its victims.

00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:49.030
It's a very creepy moment when Fred has a
hallucination of grieving mourners at a funeral

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:53.930
and a little girl points at him and her finger
extends into a long, deformed claw similar

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:56.449
to one of Vecna's giant fingers.

00:07:56.449 --> 00:08:01.169
But this original concept art suggests the
moment could have been even more gruesome,

00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:06.090
with tentacles also emerging from the girl's
arm and across her hand, and blood streaming

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.289
from her eyes.

00:08:07.289 --> 00:08:12.100
And, if you'd like to discover the super-creepy,
horrifying designs for Vecna that we almost

00:08:12.100 --> 00:08:17.050
got, including one where he had four legs
and a mantis-like body, tap here to watch

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.800
that video, or there's a link in the video
description.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:24.479
So, Movie Lovers, what do you think about
these original ideas for Season 4?

00:08:24.479 --> 00:08:26.720
Let me know in the comments below.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:31.389
If you liked this video, do leave a thumbs-up,
I really appreciate it.

00:08:31.389 --> 00:08:35.849
And you can tap left to discover every incredible
easter egg you missed in the final part of

00:08:35.849 --> 00:08:36.919
Season 4.

00:08:36.919 --> 00:08:40.780
Thanks for enjoying Stranger Things with me
and hope you have a marvellous movie-loving

00:08:40.780 --> 00:08:41.780
week!

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:42.659
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers!

